xfail = "stdout only: the usage screen names the binary ('Usage: ephpm php …' vs 'Usage: php …') and omits the flags this build does not implement (-S/-t, --repeat, --ini=diff). The behavior #336 was about — php_getopt's 'Error in argument N, char M: option not found X' on stderr, and exit 1 — now matches byte-for-byte; only the text of the usage screen differs, permanently. Pinned from the ephpm side by crates/ephpm-e2e/tests/cli.rs::unknown_option_reports_and_exits_one."
